  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nImplement manual-backed TNC DIN/ISO G200/G205/G206/G207 drilling/tapping cycles and G247 preset activation. Documented Q values distinguish absolute origin-relative surface coordinates from incremental depth/clearance. One-shot M99 calls replace only the expanded axial cuts; explicit safe links remain. No invented G80 or modal M89.\r\n\r\nAdd an explicit **Floating tap** operation choice alongside rigid **Tap**, through normal editing/undo, persisted parameters/cached cycles, CL/CNC serialization, UI and script exposure. Existing `tap`/`TAP` stays rigid. Only explicit floating-holder intent selects G206; `rigidTapping=false` refuses G207 and never implies floating tooling. Posts without the floating-tapping capability refuse that mode by name.\r\n\r\nSource: HEIDENHAIN TNC 640 Cycle Programming 892905-25, English 9/2016, NC34059x-07, sections2.1,3.3,3.8,4.2,4.3,10.4; ISO Programming manual892909-25 for block/call form. Original clean-room implementation, no vendor post source consulted. Q inventory and interface decisions: `docs/decisions/51-heidenhain-cycles.md`.\r\n\r\n## Pinned behavior and limits\r\n\r\n- G200 drilling/full-return deep drilling; G205 constant chip-breaking pecks; G206 explicit floating-holder tapping; G207 rigid tapping with machine-capability refusal.\r\n- Explicit G54..G59 maps to G247 preset rows1..6, only on change. An unstated work offset preserves the active preset. This is not TNC datum-shift G54 syntax.\r\n- Nonrepresentable R-to-entry PECK/DEEP intent retains its established explicit chain rather than deepening the first infeed. Boring chains and unrelated safety refusals remain.\r\n- Negative tapping feed/RPM is refused, not reinterpreted as handedness. G207 checks Q239 resolution; G206 checks feed resolution and the manual's0..0.5s anti-wedging dwell guidance.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nFinal commit `9261cf77c09f40742ba667bda698c690680cd750`, tested/reviewed tree `8b359ed89068b3866635a376e6a59519c3c9c60c`, integrated main `5fd45923ebffea09480e4426c05a6af0cf81e07a`. Native Windows/MSVC, locked dependencies.\r\n\r\nExecuted the **manual targeted gate** permitted by current `resolve-conflicts` step1b.5 and `work-issue` step3 (not an unrun xtask pass):\r\n\r\n- `cargo test --locked -p camcraft-app --test heidenhain_cycles --test tapping_mode --test heidenhain_block_form --test conformance --test fanuc_post --test posting --test arc_planes`: **62 passed**,0failed. Covers real generated-operation posting, mode persistence/legacy defaults/undo, Q/preset/capability/refusal, block form and all affected dialect goldens.\r\n- `cargo test --locked -p camcraft-cl --lib`: **33 passed**.\r\n- `cargo test --locked -p camcraft-post --lib`: **7 passed**.\r\n- `cargo test --locked -p camcraft-motion --lib drilling::`: **34 passed**,140filtered.\r\n- `cargo clippy --locked -p camcraft-cl -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: **exit0**, UI included.\r\n- Actual Heidenhain CLI posting of committed `drill_plate.cl`: **exit0**,15lines,10mapped records,0swallowed;425-byte output byte-equal to current drill golden.\r\n- Independent incremental static review: no required integration findings. Preserves both cycle reset and smoothing shutdown, location-aware refusal APIs, threadHands and floatingTapping, and Carvera's separate refusal.\r\n\r\nPrior full feature review and unchanged-input native evidence are retained, not represented as a fresh full run: the earlier mandatory quick/batch selected2925passing tests,1stale-G247-golden failure,30ignored. That one golden was generated and independently checked (all98prior motion bodies preserved), and its exact failed test then passed with normal assertions. The final integrated conformance/arc tests above also pass. No other-dialect golden was changed by this contribution.\r\n\r\nNo physical controller/CNC execution or transfer, release/ignored-heavy gate, other-OS test run or hosted workflow dispatch. Hosted push/PR checks are intentionally absent, not CI-green. Graphify was unavailable; no generated graph was fabricated.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nChangelog: Add documented Heidenhain native drilling/tapping cycles and preset selection, explicit floating-holder intent and backward-compatible rigid tapping.\r\n\r\nFixes #51\r\n",
